WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:09.500
In an era marked by religious decline,
Mormons appear to be holding their own.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.940
One-quarter of Americans are religiously
unaffiliated today. Among young adults,

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.220
roughly 4 in 10 are now unaffiliated.
It's a trend that's affecting nearly

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.120
every major religious
denomination in the US,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.900
with one important exception: the Church of
Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.020
The Mormon population in the US has
remained steady over the past few years,

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:33.200
even while other Christian
denominations have shed members.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.920
So, why are Mormons faring so well?
It's all about family.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.840
Mormons get married earlier,
stayed married longer, and have larger

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.880
families than members of other Christian
denominations. Mormons are also more

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.900
likely to marry within their faith than
members of most other religious traditions.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.180
82% of married Mormons report
that their spouse is also Mormon.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.000
For Mormons, family is really
fundamental. 81% of Mormons

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.110
prioritize being a good parent, and
nearly three-quarters say that having a

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:06.680
good marriage is one of their
most important life priorities.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.780
Do you think the decline of religion in
the US is a good thing or bad thing?

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.360
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know what
other topics you'd like our scholars

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.520
to cover in 60 seconds and be sure
to LIKE and subscribe

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.380
for more research and videos from AEI.

